{"id":"word:hebrew:H3603","type":"word","title":"כִּכָּר","subtitle":"H3603 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a circle , i.e. (by implication) a circumjacent tract or region, especially the Ghor or valley of the Jordan; also a (round) loaf ; also a talent (or large [round] coin )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כִּכָּר (H3603) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 68 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כִּכָּר (kikkâr) means a circle , i.e. (by implication) a circumjacent tract or region, especially the Ghor or valley of the Jordan; also a (round) loaf ; also a talent (or large [round] coin ) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כִּכָּר","transliteration":"kikkâr","pronunciation":"kik-kawr'","strong":"H3603","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3603","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["כִּכַּר","כִּכַּ֣ר","כִכַּר","כִּכַּ֥ר","הַ/כִּכָּ֔ר"],"morphs":[["HNcbsc",26],["HTd/Ncbsa",11],["HNcbsa",8],["HNcbpa",7],["HNcbpc",5],["HC/Ncbsc",4],["HR/Ncbsc",2],["HR/Ncbpa",2],["HNcbda",2],["HR/Ncbda",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a circle , i.e. (by implication) a circumjacent tract or region, especially the Ghor or valley of the Jordan; also a (round) loaf ; also a talent (or large [round] coin )","usage":"loaf, morsel, piece, plain, talent.","full":"H3603. kikkar כִּכָּר noun feminine Gen 13:10 Exod 29:32 ; a round : hence 1 a round district . 2 a round loaf . 3 a round weight, talent (Late Hebrew id.; loaf, weight, talent ; Aramaic כַּכְּרָא , talent ; Tel Amarna gaggaru kaspu Wkl No. 35, Rev. 14 Christian-Palestinian Aramaic , of honey- comb Schw Idioticon 46 ; on formative see Ba NB 204 ); — absolute ׳כ Gen 13:12 +; construct כִּכַּר 1Sam 2:36 +; dual כֶּסֶף כִּכְּרַיִם 1Kin 16:24 ; 2Kin 5:23 , כִּכָּרָ֑יִם 5:23 ; plural כִּכָּרִים 1Chr 22:14 (twice in verse) + 7 t. chr; construct כִּכְּרֵי 2Kin 5:5 2 t. Chronicles; כִּכְּרוֺת ( loaves ) Judg 8:5 ; 1Sam 10:3 ; &#8212; 1 the round (or oval ) especially of the Jordan valley, הַיַּרְדֵּן כִּכַּר Gen 13:10-11 , 1Kin 7:46 2Chr 4:17 ; absolute הַכִּכָּר Gen 19:17 , 25 ; Deut 34:3 ; 2Sam 18:23 ; הַכּ ׳אֶרֶץ Gen 19:28 ; הַכּ ׳עָרֵי 13:12 ; 19:29 , see GASm G 505 Buhl G. 112 ; district of Jerusalem, ׳הַכּ Neh 3:22 ; 12:28 . 2 loaf of bread (from round shape), לָ֑חֶם כִּכַּר 1Sam 2:36 ; Proverbs 6:36, compare Exod 29:23 ; Jer 37:21 ; 1Chr 16:3 ; לֶחֶם כִּכְּרוֺת 1Sam 10:3 ; Judg 8:5 . 3 a. a weight (also from shape), עֹפֶרֶת כִּכַּר Zech 5:7 a weight of lead , serving as cover of an ephah. b. a particularunit of weight, talent , usually of gold or silver: — זָהָבּ׳כ 2Sam 12:30 ; 2Kin 9:14 18 t.; ׳כ כֶּסֶף 1Kin 20:39 ; 2Kin 5:5 21 t.; but also of iron, בַּרְזֶל 1Chr 29:7 , and bronze נְחשֶׁת Exod 38:29 ; 1Chr 29:7 . &#8212; The weight of the talent was 58.944 kilograms (= 129.97 lbs.) according to older (Babylonian) standard, later 49.11 king (= 108.29 lbs.) and less; see Benz Archaeology 187 ff. 194Now Archaeology i. 208 f. — See also שֶׁקֶל . כרשׂ √ of following (Arabic be wrinkled ). כרר (√ of following; compare Biblical Hebrew כִּכָּר כרר, 3 ).","rootNote":"from 3769 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 16 3","keyReferences":["1Chr 16 3","1Chr 19 6","1Chr 20 2","1Chr 22 14","1Chr 22 14","1Chr 29 4","1Chr 29 4","1Chr 29 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":68,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 16 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּכַּר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 19 6","book":"1Chr","chapter":19,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּכַּר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 20 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":20,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּכַּר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 14","book":"1